# The mesh reads NVIDIA_API_KEY from the repository-root .env (../../.env),
# which compose injects into every container via `env_file`. This file just
# documents the knobs; copy the key into ../../.env.
#
#   NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...        # required — get a free key at build.nvidia.com

# Override the chat model for every specialist. RECOMMENDED: `/v1/models` lists
# models your key cannot actually call, and the catalog drifts monthly. Set an
# id confirmed callable by YOUR key. A known-good, fast Nemotron model that
# returns content directly (verified 2026-11-07):
NVIDIA_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-bolt-e4b
# Probe what your key can reach (a listed model is not necessarily callable):
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $NVIDIA_API_KEY" \
#        https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/models

# Optional: the question the CLIENT asks. (Named QUESTION, not PROMPT, so it
# doesn't collide with the shell's own $PROMPT in interactive zsh.)
# QUESTION=What is the Raft consensus algorithm, and when should I choose it over Paxos?

# Optional: log verbosity.
# RUST_LOG=info,decentralised_agents=debug

# Optional: libp2p transport knobs. Only needed when mDNS multicast is blocked
# (restricted Wi-Fi/VPN/CI). Seed one connection and discovery still flows over
# gossip. Not needed for the Docker bridge, where mDNS works.
# LISTEN=/ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/0
# BOOTSTRAP=/ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4101
